    "HULLS.TXT": "; SOVEREIGN LATTICE -- HULLS.TXT\n; Ship hull classes. Each hull borrows an original outline from INERTIA ZERO's\n; hull art (../SUBSPACE/skins.js) through its Skin key.\n;\n;   Name         Class name shown in the interface.\n;   Skin         INERTIA ZERO hull outline id.\n;   Slots        Component slots.\n;   Structure    Base hit points before armour.\n;   Speed        Base lane speed per turn (light-hours).\n;   Cost         Mineral cost of the bare hull.\n;   Requires     Technology field and level needed, e.g. \"armor 3\", or \"none\".\n;   Description  Shipyard flavour text.\n\n[HULL]\nName        = Scout\nSkin        = javelin\nSlots       = 3\nStructure   = 50\nSpeed       = 110\nCost        = 30\nRequires    = none\nDescription = A sensor mast with an engine bolted on. Built to look, not to fight.\n\n[HULL]\nName        = Corvette\nSkin        = warbird\nSlots       = 4\nStructure   = 80\nSpeed       = 95\nCost        = 55\nRequires    = none\nDescription = The workhorse escort: cheap, quick and expendable.\n\n[HULL]\nName        = Transport\nSkin        = weasel\nSlots       = 4\nStructure   = 90\nSpeed       = 85\nCost        = 50\nRequires    = none\nDescription = Wide cargo spine for colony pods and troop bays.\n\n[HULL]\nName        = Frigate\nSkin        = terrier\nSlots       = 6\nStructure   = 130\nSpeed       = 85\nCost        = 95\nRequires    = armor 1\nDescription = Twin weapon booms and enough armour to hold a lane.\n\n[HULL]\nName        = Destroyer\nSkin        = shark\nSlots       = 8\nStructure   = 190\nSpeed       = 80\nCost        = 150\nRequires    = armor 2\nDescription = Long-range line ship that sets the pace of a battle.\n\n[HULL]\nName        = Cruiser\nSkin        = lancaster\nSlots       = 11\nStructure   = 290\nSpeed       = 75\nCost        = 230\nRequires    = armor 4\nDescription = An armoured hexagon of guns. Flagship of most fleets.\n\n[HULL]\nName        = Dreadnought\nSkin        = leviathan\nSlots       = 15\nStructure   = 480\nSpeed       = 60\nCost        = 380\nRequires    = armor 6\nDescription = Slow, enormous and almost impossible to stop.\n",
    "COMPONENTS.TXT": "; SOVEREIGN LATTICE -- COMPONENTS.TXT\n; Ship components. Stats grow with the empire's level in the named field, so\n; ships upgrade automatically as research completes.\n;\n;   Name        Component name.\n;   Kind        weapon, armor, shield, engine, colony, troops or sensor.\n;   Cost        Mineral cost per component.\n;   Requires    \"field level\" or \"none\".\n;   Base        Base value (damage, hit points, shield points, speed, troops).\n;   PerLevel    Added per level of the scaling field.\n;   Scaling     Field whose level improves this component.\n;   Reload      Weapons only: fires every N combat rounds.\n;   Pierce      Weapons only: percent of shields ignored.\n;   Description Shipyard flavour text.\n\n[COMPONENT]\nName        = Pulse Laser\nKind        = weapon\nCost        = 20\nRequires    = none\nBase        = 10\nPerLevel    = 3\nScaling     = weapons\nReload      = 1\nPierce      = 0\nDescription = Reliable short bursts. Every navy starts here.\n\n[COMPONENT]\nName        = Seeker Torpedo\nKind        = weapon\nCost        = 35\nRequires    = weapons 2\nBase        = 26\nPerLevel    = 7\nScaling     = weapons\nReload      = 2\nPierce      = 0\nDescription = Heavy warhead, slow reload.\n\n[COMPONENT]\nName        = Phase Lance\nKind        = weapon\nCost        = 55\nRequires    = weapons 5\nBase        = 30\nPerLevel    = 6\nScaling     = weapons\nReload      = 1\nPierce      = 50\nDescription = Slips half its energy past enemy shields.\n\n[COMPONENT]\nName        = Hull Plating\nKind        = armor\nCost        = 12\nRequires    = none\nBase        = 30\nPerLevel    = 10\nScaling     = armor\nDescription = Layered alloy. Absorbs damage after shields fail.\n\n[COMPONENT]\nName        = Deflector\nKind        = shield\nCost        = 30\nRequires    = armor 2\nBase        = 8\nPerLevel    = 4\nScaling     = armor\nDescription = Absorbs damage every combat round, then recharges.\n\n[COMPONENT]\nName        = Ion Drive\nKind        = engine\nCost        = 15\nRequires    = none\nBase        = 25\nPerLevel    = 3\nScaling     = propulsion\nDescription = More thrust per lane.\n\n[COMPONENT]\nName        = Colony Pod\nKind        = colony\nCost        = 60\nRequires    = none\nBase        = 1\nPerLevel    = 0\nScaling     = colonization\nDescription = Settlers, seed stock and a prefabricated town. Used up on landing.\n\n[COMPONENT]\nName        = Troop Bay\nKind        = troops\nCost        = 25\nRequires    = none\nBase        = 10\nPerLevel    = 2\nScaling     = weapons\nDescription = Marines for taking defenceless colonies.\n\n[COMPONENT]\nName        = Sensor Array\nKind        = sensor\nCost        = 30\nRequires    = sensors 1\nBase        = 1\nPerLevel    = 0\nScaling     = sensors\nDescription = Lets the ship see one extra jump.\n",
    "FACILITIES.TXT": "; SOVEREIGN LATTICE -- FACILITIES.TXT\n; Colony facilities. A colony has two facility slots per point of planet size.\n;\n;   Name        Facility name.\n;   Key         Internal id used by the rules: mine, reactor, lab, shipyard,\n;               battery or habitat. Keys must stay as listed.\n;   Cost        Mineral cost.\n;   Requires    \"field level\" or \"none\".\n;   Output      Per-turn output (minerals, energy, research), defence or pop %.\n;   Description Flavour text.\n\n[FACILITY]\nName        = Deep Mine\nKey         = mine\nCost        = 60\nRequires    = none\nOutput      = 12\nDescription = +12 minerals per turn.\n\n[FACILITY]\nName        = Fusion Reactor\nKey         = reactor\nCost        = 60\nRequires    = none\nOutput      = 12\nDescription = +12 energy per turn.\n\n[FACILITY]\nName        = Research Lab\nKey         = lab\nCost        = 80\nRequires    = none\nOutput      = 10\nDescription = +10 research per turn.\n\n[FACILITY]\nName        = Orbital Shipyard\nKey         = shipyard\nCost        = 120\nRequires    = none\nOutput      = 0\nDescription = Builds ships. One per colony.\n\n[FACILITY]\nName        = Defence Battery\nKey         = battery\nCost        = 90\nRequires    = none\nOutput      = 120\nDescription = Planetary guns and shields: +120 defence.\n\n[FACILITY]\nName        = Arcology\nKey         = habitat\nCost        = 140\nRequires    = colonization 2\nOutput      = 25\nDescription = +25% maximum population.\n",
